  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A fly wheel is accelerated uniformly from rest and rotates through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>rad</mi></math> in the first second. The angle rotated by the fly wheel in the next second, will be :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3vAqh",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Hg7Ty",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "G39Px",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iQqH9",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>rad</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here the angular acceleration is constant, so we have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>When flywheel is rotated from rest in the first second, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The angle turned by flywheel in the next second is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Thus, the angle turned during next second&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi></math></p>",
